{"name":"Spirit Rock","hex":"#5f534e","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spirit","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The soul of a person or other creature.","A supernatural being, often but not exclusively without physical form; ghost, fairy, angel."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To carry off, especially in haste, secrecy, or mystery.","Sometimes followed by up: to animate with vigour; to excite; to encourage; to inspirit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spirit"},{"term":"rock","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A formation of minerals, specifically.","A mass of stone projecting out of the ground or water."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To pelt with rocks; to stone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rock"}],"entries":[{"title":"Senior rock","blocks":[{"text":"The senior rock is a rural and suburban United States tradition in which youth, often a high school senior class, paint a prominent local rock with class colors, graduating year, or names of the members of the class. A rock at Northwestern University is said to have \"inches of paint after 80 years of the tradition\". The tradition may have started in the 1950s or 1960s at universities and high schools."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/UNCW_Fisher_Student_Union_and_Spirit_Rock.jpg/330px-UNCW_Fisher_Student_Union_and_Spirit_Rock.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Senior_rock","wikidata":"Q65040228"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/UNCW_Fisher_Student_Union_and_Spirit_Rock.jpg/500px-UNCW_Fisher_Student_Union_and_Spirit_Rock.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/UNCW_Fisher_Student_Union_and_Spirit_Rock.jpg/1280px-UNCW_Fisher_Student_Union_and_Spirit_Rock.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/UNCW_Fisher_Student_Union_and_Spirit_Rock.jpg/500px-UNCW_Fisher_Student_Union_and_Spirit_Rock.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A \"spirit rock\" at University of North Carolina at Wilmington","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUNCW_Fisher_Student_Union_and_Spirit_Rock.jpg"}],"sounds":{"spirit":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f7/En-us-spirit.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/f7/En-us-spirit.ogg/En-us-spirit.ogg.mp3"}],"rock":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/25/En-us-rock.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/25/En-us-rock.ogg/En-us-rock.ogg.mp3"}]}}}